#: src/ai/rules.md:3 src/ai/rules.md:55
msgid "Using Rules"
msgstr "使用規則"

#: src/ai/rules.md:5
msgid ""
"Rules are prompts that can be inserted either automatically at the beginning "
"of each [Agent Panel](./agent-panel.md) interaction, through `.rules` files "
"available in your project's file tree, or on-demand, through @-mentioning, "
"via the Rules Library."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/rules.md:7
msgid "`.rules` files"
msgstr "`.rules` 檔案"

#: src/ai/rules.md:9
msgid ""
"Zed supports including `.rules` files at the root of a project's file tree, "
"and they act as project-level instructions that are auto-included in all of "
"your interactions with the Agent Panel."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/rules.md:11
msgid ""
"Other names for this file are also supported for compatibility with other "
"agents, but note that the first file which matches in this list will be used:"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/rules.md:13
msgid "`.rules`"
msgstr "`.rules`"

#: src/ai/rules.md:14
msgid "`.cursorrules`"
msgstr "`.cursorrules`"

#: src/ai/rules.md:15
msgid "`.windsurfrules`"
msgstr "`.windsurfrules`"

#: src/ai/rules.md:16
msgid "`.clinerules`"
msgstr "`.clinerules`"

#: src/ai/rules.md:17
msgid "`.github/copilot-instructions.md`"
msgstr "`.github/copilot-instructions.md`"

#: src/ai/rules.md:18
msgid "`AGENT.md`"
msgstr "`AGENT.md`"

#: src/ai/rules.md:19
msgid "`AGENTS.md`"
msgstr "`AGENTS.md`"

#: src/ai/rules.md:20
msgid "`CLAUDE.md`"
msgstr "`CLAUDE.md`"

#: src/ai/rules.md:21
msgid "`GEMINI.md`"
msgstr "`GEMINI.md`"

#: src/ai/rules.md:23
msgid "Rules Library"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/rules.md:25
msgid ""
"The Rules Library is an interface for writing and managing rules. It's a "
"full editor with syntax highlighting and all standard keybindings."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/rules.md:28
msgid ""
"You can also use the inline assistant right in the rules editor, allowing "
"you to get quick LLM support for writing rules."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/rules.md:30
msgid "Opening the Rules Library"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/rules.md:32
msgid "Open the Agent Panel."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/rules.md:33
msgid "Click on the Agent menu (`...`) in the top right corner."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/rules.md:34
msgid "Select `Rules...` from the dropdown."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/rules.md:36
msgid ""
"You can also open it by running the <code class=\"hljs\">agent: open rules "
"library</code> action or through the <kbd class=\"keybinding\">cmd-alt-l|"
"ctrl-alt-l</kbd> keybinding."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/rules.md:38
msgid "Managing Rules"
msgstr "管理規則"

#: src/ai/rules.md:40
msgid ""
"Once a rules file is selected, you can edit it directly in the built-in "
"editor. Its title can be changed from the editor title bar as well."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/rules.md:43
msgid ""
"Rules can be duplicated, deleted, or added to the default rules using the "
"buttons in the rules editor."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/rules.md:45
msgid "Creating Rules"
msgstr "建立規則"

#: src/ai/rules.md:47
msgid ""
"To create a rule file, simply open the `Rules Library` and click the `+` "
"button. Rules files are stored locally and can be accessed from the library "
"at any time."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/rules.md:50
msgid "For guidance on writing effective rules:"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/rules.md:52
msgid ""
"[Anthropic: Prompt Engineering](https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/build-"
"with-claude/prompt-engineering/overview)"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/rules.md:53
msgid ""
"[OpenAI: Prompt Engineering](https://platform.openai.com/docs/guides/prompt-"
"engineering)"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/rules.md:57
msgid ""
"You can @-mention every rule created through the Rules Library. This allows "
"you to quickly reach for reusable prompts, saving the time to type them out "
"every time you need to use them."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/rules.md:60
msgid "Default Rules"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/rules.md:62
msgid ""
"All rules in the Rules Library can be set as a default rule, which means "
"they’re automatically inserted into context for every new Agent Panel "
"interaction."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/rules.md:64
msgid ""
"You can set any rule as the default by clicking the paper clip icon button "
"in the top-right of the rule editor in the Rules Library."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/rules.md:66
msgid "Migrating from Prompt Library"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/rules.md:68
msgid ""
"Previously, the Rules Library was called the \"Prompt Library\". The new "
"rules system replaces the Prompt Library except in a few specific cases, "
"which are outlined below."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/rules.md:71
msgid "Slash Commands in Rules"
msgstr "規則中的斜線命令"

#: src/ai/rules.md:73
msgid ""
"Previously, it was possible to use slash commands (now @-mentions) in custom "
"prompts (now rules). There is currently no support for using @-mentions in "
"rules files, however, slash commands are supported in rules files when used "
"with text threads. See the documentation for using [slash commands in rules]"
"(./text-threads.md#slash-commands-in-rules) for more information."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/rules.md:77
msgid "Prompt templates"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/rules.md:79
msgid ""
"Zed maintains backwards compatibility with its original template system, "
"which allows you to customize prompts used throughout the application, "
"including the inline assistant. While the Rules Library is now the primary "
"way to manage prompts, you can still use these legacy templates to override "
"default prompts. For more details, see the [Rules Templates](./text-threads."
"md#rule-templates) section under [Text Threads](./text-threads.md)."
msgstr ""
